abstract: >-
  This archive holds the oracle implementations, verification scripts, and evidence behind a paper
  on fault-class-matched test oracles for quantum transpiler regressions. A companion empirical
  study finds that roughly 28% of merged Qiskit transpiler bug-fixes repair a fault that corrupts
  layout/permutation metadata, global phase, or run-to-run determinism while the executed output
  stays correct, invisible to a standard output-equivalence oracle by construction. This paper
  introduces a matched oracle family, a layout/permutation contract checker and a contract-level
  metamorphic relation for the metadata channel, a global-phase tracker for the phase channel, and
  a determinism runner for the reproducibility channel, and verifies it from source on nine real,
  merged Qiskit transpiler regressions (three per channel), on synthetic mutant families built to
  each channel's own invariant, and on a native port of the global-phase mechanism to pytket/tket.
  The archive includes every verification script, the oracle source code, the already-executed
  result files each reported number traces to, and the environment/build protocol needed to
  rebuild any of it from source.
